package concept

point_charge: {
  content: #"""
    A *point charge* is an idealized model of a charged object whose size is
    small enough to ignore for the question being studied. We treat its entire
    charge $q$ as if it were located at one point in space.

    This model is useful when the object's dimensions are much smaller than
    its distance from the places where we want to describe its electric
    effects. A charged sphere viewed from far away, for example, can often be
    approximated as a point charge with the same total charge.

    A point charge is a simplification of the object's size and shape. It does
    not mean that charge itself has become continuous or that the object must
    literally have no size. When the object's size matters, we describe how its
    charge is spread using a continuous charge distribution.
  """#
  related: [
    "concept/quantization-of-electric-charge",
    "concept/continuous-charge-distribution"
  ]
}
